WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.090
This year, I gave a keynote
in Porto Alegre, Brazil.

2
00:00:04.550 --> 00:00:08.730
Building AI innovation with
healthcare, not simply for it.

3
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:12.880
In 2025, I went to Capitol Hill
with workforce-development leaders,

4
00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:16.830
to talk about workforce technology
and the jobs coming next.

5
00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:19.510
Before that, AI in education.

6
00:00:19.820 --> 00:00:24.250
Twice at TCEA in Austin,
on the skepticism, and the safety.

7
00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:27.620
ZoneSight at IEEE EDUCON, in London.

8
00:00:27.640 --> 00:00:31.930
And motivation and the adolescent
brain, for teachers in Jacksonville.

9
00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:35.590
In 2015, at the Hintsa
Performance Clinic in Geneva,

10
00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:38.950
I presented NeuRace, the
company I founded and led.

11
00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:43.120
Our machine-learning pipeline read
a driver's brain and body signals live,

12
00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:44.950
next to the car's telemetry.

13
00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:47.650
That talk started our
collaboration with Hintsa.

14
00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:50.370
In 2012, TEDx Abu Dhabi.

15
00:00:50.620 --> 00:00:52.970
Music, neuroscience, and education,

16
00:00:53.180 --> 00:00:55.450
and what we can learn
from the spaces between.

17
00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:58.710
And the first talk on
my list, from 2010.

18
00:00:59.150 --> 00:01:01.270
Barcelona, Human Brain Mapping.

19
00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:04.350
White matter, and what
musical training does to it.

20
00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:06.970
I do keynotes, panels, and workshops.

21
00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:10.390
My favorite ones feel more like
a jam session than a lecture.

22
00:01:10.580 --> 00:01:12.810
If you're putting something
together, let's talk.
